REGIONAL REGULATION OF BEKASI REGENCY

NUMBER 5 OF 2020

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF BEKASI,

Considering:

a. that women are assets who play a very important role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations so they need to receive protection guarantees from acts of violence and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;
b. that in order to realize the fulfillment of women's constitutional rights to be free from torture, treatment that degrades human dignity, the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all violence and to improve the quality of life of women, they need to receive protection and empowerment from the regional government of Bekasi Regency;
C. that the implementation of protection of women in Bekasi Regency has not been able to be carried out optimally and is accompanied by violations of women's rights so that a comprehensive regulation is needed to provide direction, foundation, and legal certainty;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women;

In View of:

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of 1950) as amended by Law Number 4 of 1968 concerning the Establishment of Purwakarta Regency and Bekasi Regency by Amending Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1968 Number 31, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2851);
3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1948 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277;
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3886;
5. Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419;
6. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635) as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5602;
7. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 144, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5063);
8. Law Number 19 of 2011 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Rights of Persons With Disabilities (Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 107, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5251);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 567;
10. Law Number 8 of 2016 concerning Persons with Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 69, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5871);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BEKASI REGENCY

and

REGENT OF BEKASI

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN

Article 2

1. Women have the right:
a. to live;
b. to form a family and continue descendants;
c. to self-development;
d. to obtain justice;
e. to personal freedom;
f. to a sense of security;
g. to welfare; and
h. to participate in government.
2. Every woman has the right:
a. to live peacefully, safely, in peace, happily, prosperously both physically and spiritually;
b. to be free from all threats of violence and/or exploitation;
c. to live in a family within the bonds of a lawful marriage;
d. to maintain life and improve her standard of living;
e. to have work that she likes and is also entitled to fair employment conditions;
f. to obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education in accordance with the specified requirements;
g. to a healthy and clean environment;
h. to receive fair wages in accordance with her work that is comparable and commensurate with human dignity;
i. to elect and/or be elected in general elections, regional head elections, village head elections and/or other political office elections based on equal rights through direct, general, free, secret, honest and fair voting in accordance with applicable laws and regulations;
j. to obtain special protection in the implementation of work or profession against matters that may threaten safety and/or health related to women's reproductive function; and
k. special rights inherent to women due to their reproductive function are guaranteed and protected by law.
l. to obtain legal protection and assistance for problems faced in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
m. other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
3. Every woman with disabilities, elderly, pregnant is entitled to obtain facilities and special treatment.
4. Every elderly woman, with physical and/or mental disabilities, is entitled to obtain care, education, training and special assistance from the Regional Government to ensure a decent life in accordance with human dignity.
5. The Regional Government strives for an old age protection guarantee system for elderly women.

Article 3

Every woman with disabilities has the right:
a. to reproductive health;
b. to accept or refuse the use of contraceptives;
c. to obtain greater protection from multiple discrimination;
d. to obtain greater protection from acts of violence, including sexual violence and exploitation;
e. to obtain education in all units, pathways, types and levels of education;
f. to obtain decent work and livelihood in accordance with the type and degree of disability, education and ability;
g. to obtain accessibility in the context of independence;
h. to obtain rehabilitation, social assistance and maintenance of social welfare standards; and
i. to obtain equal rights to develop talents, abilities and social life.

Article 4

Every woman victim of violence has the right to:
a. obtain protection;
b. determine her own decisions;
c. obtain information;
d. obtain complaint handling;
e. obtain assistance;
f. obtain continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage; and
g. obtain confidential handling from individuals, groups or institutions, both government and non-government.

CHAPTER III

FORMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 8

Forms of violence include:
a. Physical Violence;
b. Psychological Violence;
c. Sexual Violence; and
d. Domestic Violence;

Article 11

1. Sexual Violence as referred to in Article 8 letter c is caused by:
a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. sexual abuse;
c. coercion of unnatural or unwanted sexual relations;
d. coercion of sexual relations with others and/or exploitation of women for commercial purposes and other specific purposes.
2. Coercion of sexual relations as referred to in article 11 paragraph (1) letter c is excluded for persons with mental disorders or sexual deviations in marital relations.

Article 13

1. The Regional Government undertakes integrated efforts to prevent violence against women in the Region.
2. The integrated efforts to prevent violence against women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be coordinated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for the protection and empowerment of women. (3) The prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be implemented by:
a. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns that may involve community organizations, universities, professionals as well as customary heads and/or community leaders;
b. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of the rights of women victims of violence;
c. establishing an integrated violence prevention system;
d. providing ease of access to obtain civil rights, education, health, employment, training and funding, welfare improvement and social services;
e. providing education regarding women's rights to the community;
f. fostering and developing community participation and concern for the protection of women from acts of violence;
g. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system; and
h. establishing a cooperation network in prevention efforts from acts of violence with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women.

Article 14

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 13, shall be implemented by the Regional Apparatus responsible for:
a. health;
b. education;
c. employment;
d. socio-political affairs;
e. protection and empowerment of women; and
f. peace and order;
2. Prevention of acts of violence by the Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan with the Regional Apparatus responsible for the Protection and Empowerment of Women.
